 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Though, in a little walk by river,\nThe lovers' love was sharpest to behold;\nBut 'twere not their rosy lips they behold\nMore clearly than the last happy hour.\nThey kissed and parted as pales depart,\nWith oneness new-sprung from sepulchre!  Instead\nOf throwing out a joyful farewell to\nA garland for another's grave beside.\nAnd such is the one-day love between\nWho give each other joys of eternal;\nBut when there are no more present flowers,\nNo further wedded lives remaineth. O",
